    </script>
  </Fragment>
    <Nav>
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <a href="/free-nextjs-hosting">Free hosting</a>
          <a href="/vercel-alternative">vs Vercel</a>
          <a href="/docs" class="keep">Docs</a>
    </Nav>

    <div class="container docs">
      <aside class="toc">
        <p class="toc-title">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#included">What you get</a></li>
          <li><a href="#create">Create a database</a></li>
          <li><a href="#connect">Connect from your app</a></li>
          <li><a href="#prisma">Prisma migrations</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cli">Query from the CLI</a></li>
          <li><a href="#limits">Limits and caveats</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>

      <main class="doc">
        <div class="doc-head">
          <ol class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <li><a href="/">EasyHost</a></li><li aria-current="page">Free Postgres hosting</li>
          </ol>
          <h1>Free Postgres hosting that comes with your app</h1>
          <p class="lead">Every EasyHost project can have one free Postgres 16 database. You get a standard connection string over TLS, a separate shadow database for Prisma, and a CLI that can run SQL. There is no credit card, and the database is not deleted on a timer.</p>
          <p class="doc-meta">Last updated November 9, 2026</p>
        </div>

        <section id="included">
          <h2>What the free Postgres database includes</h2>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Engine</td><td>Postgres 16</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Databases</td><td>1 per project, up to 3 projects per account</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Access</td><td>Your own database and role, reachable from anywhere over TLS</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Connections</td><td>Up to 20 at a time per database</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Shadow database</td><td>Included, for <code>prisma migrate dev</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Tools</td><td>SQL from the CLI, plus a table browser and editor in the dashboard</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Expiry</td><td>None</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Price</td><td>$0</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>The connection string works with any Postgres client, so you can use the database from your EasyHost app, from your laptop, or from an app hosted somewhere else.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="create">
          <h2>Create a database</h2>
          <div class="code"><pre>npx ezhst db create main
npx ezhst db info --json
npx ezhst env set DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..."
npx ezhst redeploy</pre></div>
          <p><code>db info</code> returns the connection string and the shadow connection string. Setting <code>DATABASE_URL</code> with <code>env set</code> makes it available to your app on the next deploy. A coding agent with the <a href="/guides/deploy-nextjs-with-ai-agents">EasyHost skill</a> does all four steps when you ask it to "add a Postgres database".</p>
        </section>

        <section id="connect">
          <h2>Connect from your Next.js app</h2>
          <p>Use whichever client you already use. With Drizzle:</p>
          <div class="code"><div class="code-label">lib/db.ts</div><pre>import &#123; drizzle &#125; from "drizzle-orm/node-postgres";

export const db = drizzle(process.env.DATABASE_URL!);</pre></div>
          <p>With Prisma, <code>DATABASE_URL</code> is read from the datasource block in <code>schema.prisma</code> as usual.</p>
          <p>Because your app is a long-running Node.js process rather than a set of serverless functions, a normal connection pool works and you do not need a pooling proxy in front of the database.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="prisma">
          <h2>Prisma migrations and the shadow database</h2>
          <p><code>prisma migrate dev</code> needs a second, empty database to detect drift. On a host that gives you a single database, you have to find one somewhere else. EasyHost creates it for you and returns its URL from <code>ezhst db info</code>.</p>
          <div class="code"><div class="code-label">prisma/schema.prisma</div><pre>datasource db &#123;
  provider          = "postgresql"
  url               = env("DATABASE_URL")
  shadowDatabaseUrl = env("SHADOW_DATABASE_URL")
&#125;</pre></div>
          <p>Run migrations from your machine against the connection string, for example <code>prisma migrate deploy</code> before a deploy.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="cli">
          <h2>Query it from the command line</h2>
          <div class="cmds">
            <div class="cmd-row"><code>ezhst db query "select count(*) from users"</code><span>Run one SQL statement.</span></div>
            <div class="cmd-row"><code>ezhst db query --file seed.sql</code><span>Run a SQL file.</span></div>
            <div class="cmd-row"><code>ezhst db rows users --page 2</code><span>Browse rows in a table.</span></div>
            <div class="cmd-row"><code>ezhst db reset-password</code><span>Rotate the password and print the new connection string.</span></div>
          </div>
          <p>All of them accept <code>--json</code>, which is how agents inspect a schema or check that a migration worked. Statements run through the CLI and dashboard time out after 15 seconds. See the <a href="/docs#database">database docs</a> for every command.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="limits">
          <h2>Limits and caveats</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>One database per project. Create another project if you need a second one.</li>
            <li>Databases live on a shared Postgres server in one region. This is meant for side projects, prototypes and small apps, not for heavy production workloads.</li>
            <li>Each database allows up to 20 concurrent connections.</li>
            <li>Keep your own backups of anything important. <code>pg_dump</code> works with the connection string.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>For comparison, Render's free Postgres databases expire 30 days after creation and are capped at 1 GB, according to the <a href="https://render.com/docs/free" rel="noopener">Render free tier docs</a> as of September 2026.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="faq">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <h3>Is the EasyHost Postgres database free forever?</h3>
          <p>It is free with no trial period and no expiry date. Each project can have one database.</p>
          <h3>Can I connect from outside EasyHost?</h3>
          <p>Yes. The connection string uses a public host with TLS, so it works from your laptop, from CI and from apps hosted elsewhere.</p>
          <h3>Does it work with Prisma and Drizzle?</h3>
          <p>Yes. It is a standard Postgres 16 database. A shadow database for <code>prisma migrate dev</code> is included.</p>
          <h3>Can I use the database without hosting an app on EasyHost?</h3>
          <p>Yes. Create a project, create its database and use the connection string anywhere. You do not have to deploy an app to the project.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="start">
          <h2>Start for free</h2>
          <p>Install the skill, choose Global or Local, then tell your agent to deploy. No credit card, no config files.</p>
          <div class="code"><pre>npx ezhst skill install</pre></div>
          <div class="doc-cta">
            <a href="https://app.easyhost.fun/register" class="btn btn-primary">Sign up free</a>
            <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-outline">Read the docs</a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>
    <Footer />
    <CopyCode />
</Base>
